[
  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-121242",
      "knowledge_point_id": "798800a5-255a-5738-91d2-21c2a78e4fb5",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table",
      "problem": "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=-5x{y}^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-5x$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/743df5f5c9232346866a01aed9afa3d41fff0f61bf7812b7ae5db9a43efe59f4.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
