  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-6880",
      "knowledge_point_id": "db20f4a5-27a4-5fbc-aae2-2febf8f99cb1",
      "knowledge_point": "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at the Origin",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/86dcfa13b7863c08b348855e776a6df709ecac499af02c2479cfdf484eeaf328.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate the ellipse shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=4$ and $b=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-6880",
        "kp_title": "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at the Origin",
