  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-106408",
      "knowledge_point_id": "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262",
      "knowledge_point": "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse",
      "problem": "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2 \\\\ x-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(x-2) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3 \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(y-3) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{(y-3)}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2}=1.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "4{(x-2)}^{2}-4{(y-3)}^{2}=1",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{4}{(x-2)}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{(y-3)}^{2}=1",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2}=1",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{4}{(x-2)}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{(y-3)}^{2}=1",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "4{(x-3)}^{2}+4{(y-2)}^{2}=1",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "hard",
