  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-75992",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities",
      "problem": "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}-2x+15>0.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-2x+15>0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-2x+15\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-2x+15 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}+2x-15) & =0 \\\\ -(x+5)(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-5$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/da88a1971a7a389c8f5b59ebd3cef2a146eb09113c3e71031bf9dfb6cdbe91e1.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-5<x<3.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-3<x<5",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$x<-3$ or $x>5$",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x>-5",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$x<-5$ or $x>3$",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-5<x<3",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-75992",
        "kp_title": "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities",
        "kp_href": null
      },
      "topic_id": 3833,
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/state.json",
      "source_answer_status": "under_review",
      "assets": [
        {
          "path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/da88a1971a7a389c8f5b59ebd3cef2a146eb09113c3e71031bf9dfb6cdbe91e1.png",
