  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-142180",
      "knowledge_point_id": "ef5d4f19-5602-54a9-96ea-4e42054ff5c8",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Greater Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities",
      "problem": "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}+9x-18\\ge 0.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+9x-18\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+9x-18\n$$\n\nlies *above* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+9x-18 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-9x+18) & =0 \\\\ -(x-3)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=3$ and $x=6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/d4c28d26425c3c5bfc95dece73c8d8cb74f395f2de04a2c2ee1b1fd69f8433ed.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *above* the axis or touches the $x$-axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $3\\le x\\le 6.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$x<3$ or $x>6$",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3<x<6",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$x\\le 3$ or $x\\ge 6$",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3\\le x\\le 6",
