  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-3881",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement",
      "problem": "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}\\ge -4x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2} & \\ge -4x \\\\ -{x}^{2}+4x & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-{x}^{2}+4x$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ -x(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/d234c29de2a39c664d6a03acf1d8cc43782914a3c82045cc103353ebaf67b897.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+4x\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,4].$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [-4,4]",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-\\infty ,0]\\cup [4,\\infty )",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [-4,0]",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [0,4]",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]\\cup [0,\\infty )",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
