  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-3951",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement",
      "problem": "Find the solution of $2{x}^{2}-12\\le -5x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-12 & \\le -5x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=2{x}^{2}+5x-12$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x-12 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}+8x)+(-3x-12) & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+4)-3(x+4) & =0 \\\\ (2x-3)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004892/assets/ba6c384800a5b42f2033527997328aa9f9d792b33b3fabecfe9b3a93789f46c4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n \n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+5x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\n we look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\n Based on the graph, the solution is $-4\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-4,\\frac{3}{2}].$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [-4,\\frac{3}{2}]",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [-\\frac{1}{2},2]",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [0,2]",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [-1,\\frac{8}{3}]",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\in [\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{11}{3}]",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
